{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-universal-homeomorphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a07bb346fb3b8a2c9985282f7fa56619acfc9423bc66525cd6b2506ac6d7c18f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6bbea0d230737c7f0b5ede225b9ee6f1e67b421c86bac9688990eef24f1a3608", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. The following are\nequivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is a universal homeomorphism, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is integral, universally injective and surjective.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2b5d97cae9b65130a46fa4a16bec92ae66ddb0be5a07caaf6b40af9256b97735", "unit_id": "tag:04DF:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-homeomorphism-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-integral-universally-closed}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-integral-universally-closed}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-surjective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:41212245937bd4f663db1ec15d29b9cd2a76817a2da5ef848a0e8d1d7b90c7bc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6ecd8a1cb23a7ae31d65a8432560cf9ffd009cba50a51b12ac60790d763ad233", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> is a universal homeomorphism. By\nLemma <REF_0001>\nwe see that <MATH_0002> is affine. Since <MATH_0003> is clearly universally closed we\nsee that <MATH_0004> is integral by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nIt is also clear that <MATH_0005> is universally injective and surjective.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume <MATH_0006> is integral, universally injective and surjective. By\nLemma <REF_0003>\n<MATH_0007> is universally closed. Since it is also universally bijective (see\nLemma <REF_0004>)\nwe see that it is a universal homeomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aca0fb2a07c209eeb59c51ec2e93ad49ff6b2519ebcfb4ed05a7515472f12f30", "unit_id": "tag:04DF:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04DC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X_{red} \\to X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-definition-reduced-induced-scheme}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-reduction-universal-homeomorphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:16632493a8d4e2c8d8905cbb43563fa9cfc0b43b5c6f36a6a9ef0f7740c4df06", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:820c4736fa31412e3a1da60dbce1e84fa6ec11613202926d17c3247afb07d6f8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The canonical closed immersion <MATH_0002> (see\nSchemes, Definition <REF_0001>)\nis a universal homeomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:71aebfc14668f1d80f06e4f377c6607662faa20b7752f2af3c29f38fa785a322", "unit_id": "tag:054M:statement"}
